{:edb/db-before-t 1430 :edb/db-after-t 1431 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534743 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:39:06.142Z" 13194139534743 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307055 13194139534743 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307069 13194139534743 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307062 13194139534743 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307075 13194139534743 true] [17592186307055 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307056 13194139534743 true] [17592186307055 1089 "q-102664" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307055 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534743 true] [17592186307055 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=1-2t,\\,\\,\\,y=(t-2)^{2}(t+1),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307055 1113 #uuid "9907e86a-7f0e-52ec-b8f3-600094230c4d" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307055 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1-2t\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{1-x}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{1-x}{2}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{1-x}{2}-2)}^{2}(\\frac{1-x}{2}+1) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1-x-4}{2})}^{2}(\\frac{1-x+2}{2}) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-x-3}{2})}^{2}(\\frac{3-x}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)^{2}(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=-\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)^{2}(x-3).$" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307057 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307058 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307059 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307060 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307061 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1041 "selection" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307060 13194139534743 true] [17592186307056 1110 #uuid "be0e7474-ddca-5d74-85f5-84048b123a20" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307057 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{2}(x+3)^{2}(x-3)" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307057 1111 #uuid "ceee72aa-ee31-5323-8443-523f2234a0ce" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307058 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{4}(x+3)(x-3)^{2}" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307058 1111 #uuid "8452cb91-7694-52d5-a8f7-64a61f1c102c" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307059 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)(x-3)^{2}" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307059 1111 #uuid "2c47a2dc-1e64-54ee-9a80-14d0dca49ca9" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307060 1034 "y=-\\frac{1}{8}(x+3)^{2}(x-3)" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307060 1111 #uuid "f82d2a4d-807f-5a5c-93fa-f6f20429dd11" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307061 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+3)^{2}(x-3)" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307061 1111 #uuid "c4a63922-2589-5ebc-bba0-9c8f77371341" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307062 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307063 13194139534743 true] [17592186307062 1089 "q-24575" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307062 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534743 true] [17592186307062 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307062 1113 #uuid "a1295497-95f0-563c-9b4d-4d497affdde7" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307062 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\frac{x}{3} \\\\ y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\frac{x}{3}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{4}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{4} & =2{(-\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{4} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1 \\\\ y & =4(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=4(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1).$" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307064 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307065 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307066 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307067 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307068 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1041 "selection" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307066 13194139534743 true] [17592186307063 1110 #uuid "1d956d25-b226-5c60-804c-520274c8dd5f" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307064 1034 "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307064 1111 #uuid "f94cb9c0-1aef-5920-9e36-292ab6763aa4" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307065 1034 "y=7(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+1)" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307065 1111 #uuid "e997ce2d-a1d4-59a7-b20d-754d3ed14510" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307066 1034 "y=4(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{9}-1)" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307066 1111 #uuid "c541779d-bbe7-5c87-8f30-1ed1b67ea24f" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307067 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-1" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307067 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307067 1111 #uuid "e55f241a-779f-5e97-b1b7-f13353144ee3" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307068 1034 "y=1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307068 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534743 true] [17592186307068 1111 #uuid "ca950cea-4977-5929-b108-f1f297fada93" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307070 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307073 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1089 "q-320926" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{t}{-2t+1},\\,t\\ne -3,\\,\\,\\,t\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ne $\n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.$" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1113 #uuid "68b75bd8-3590-5aaa-ab0b-d5ba8601a2b1" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307069 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t+3}\\,⇒\\,t=-3+\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=-3+\\frac{1}{x}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-3+\\frac{1}{x})}{(-2\\,(-3+\\frac{1}{x})+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3+\\frac{1}{x})}{(6-\\frac{2}{x}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3+\\frac{1}{x})}{(7-\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3x+1}{\\cancel{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{x}}{7x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2}.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ne \\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{1}{t+3}$ has range $x\\ne 0,$ we must have \n$x\\ne \\frac{2}{7},\\text{ }0.$ \n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1-3x}{7x-2},\\,x\\ne \\frac{2}{7},\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$" 13194139534743 true] [17592186307070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307071 13194139534743 true] [17592186307070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307072 13194139534743 true] [17592186307070 1040 #edb/ref 1759218604